  "privacyTitle": "Privacy",
  "privacyTooltip": "How we know this is true",
  "privacyBody": "What you just told us, and everything your Kind taps next, stays here. Lighthouse has no account and never sends your child's Wörter anywhere.",
  "howWeKnowTitle": "How we know",
  "howWeKnowBody1": "Lighthouse does not connect to any cloud. There is no analytics SDK in the app. There is no automatic Absturz reporting. Data leaves the device only when you choose to send it: if you Tippen \"Send Absturz logs\", which opens your own mail app pre-addressed to us so you can review and Tippen send, or if you Teilen a vocabulary Tafel with another family, where you pick the destination. You stay in control either way; nothing is sent automatically.",
  "howWeKnowBody2": "You can verify this on the Einstellungen screen, which lets you preview the exact Absturz log contents before you send. A Absturz log holds the device model, the OS Version, and a technical Fehler report (the Fehler type, its message, and the code trace). The app is built not to Aufnehmen the Wörter your Kind taps or your Tafel content, and because you preview each log and choose whether to send it, you stay in control of what leaves the device.",
  "howWeKnowUpdates": "If you Tippen \"Check for updates\", the app sends only its Version number to ask whether corrected Wörter, pictures, or sounds are available. It sends nothing Über your Kind or how the app is used.",
  "howWeKnowFeedback": "If you Tippen \"Send feedback\", the app sends only the message you write, plus the app and system Version. The message is not stored, and it carries nothing Über your Kind or your boards.",
